9
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:26,100
♫Where’s that love people are saying?♫

10
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,500
♫To always be by each other’s sides♫

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,580
♫The love that’s willing to sacrifice everything♫

12
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,580
♫Everything even my own life♫

13
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:39,060
♫Do they really exist? I’d rather not believe it♫

14
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,140
♫I don’t think I’ll ever fall for anyone♫

15
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,380
♫Love? I don’t find it interesting♫

16
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,460
♫Sorry about that♫

17
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,500
♫But then who are you?♫

18
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,500
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

19
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,900
♫Please tell me♫

20
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:01,220
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

21
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:04,580
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

22
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,660
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

23
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,740
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

24
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:14,100
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

25
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,380
♫Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

26
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,580
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

27
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,460
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

28
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,340
♫Is it you?♫

29
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,060
♫Is it you?♫

30
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:35,620
[Flaming Chains of Love]

31
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:38,330
[Previously]
Are you and Fai seeing each other?

32
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:39,570
- No!
- No, Boss Rose!

33
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,700
There’s no way I’d be interested in this girl.

34
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:43,570
What you said was nothing but rude.

35
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:46,270
I’m sorry I said those things to you.

36
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:47,670
It’s okay. I’m used to it.

37
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:49,270
I’m really sorry.

38
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:50,900
Isn’t she pretty, Fai?

39
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:51,900
She’s just okay.

40
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,580
Men will be lining up to talk to her.

41
00:01:53,729 --> 00:01:54,530
Are you Kaphrao?

42
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:56,580
Nod!

43
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,180
Phrao!

44
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,970
You two seem really close.

45
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,820
We played together, ate together, and even slept on the same bed.

46
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:03,770
Let’s go talk in your room after this.

47
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:05,580
You can just stay over in my room.

48
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:10,380
I plan to build an accommodation there. I want you and Kaphrao to take a look at it.

49
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:11,170
That’s all right.

50
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:12,600
I go there quite often.

51
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:14,180
I already have an idea what needs to be done.

52
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:15,520
I want to go there.

53
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,220
Wow!

54
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:19,530
We’re almost there.

55
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:21,320
-  Where is it?
- Over there.

56
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,750
- Off you go.
- Careful there.

57
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:53,280
Dad, let’s go. Hurry up.

58
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,850
Yeah, yeah, I’m coming.

59
00:02:57,579 --> 00:02:58,300
Careful, Dad.

60
00:02:58,470 --> 00:02:59,620
You come up too.

61
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:01,280
- Yeah.
- Come, let me help.

62
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:03,720
- Let’s go.
- Let’s go, Dad.

63
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:05,650
Hurry up, Dad. Be careful too.

64
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:11,400
Oh, hi, Aunt Ju!

65
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:12,730
Aren’t you a sight for sore eyes?

66
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,370
Aw, I’m flattered.

67
00:03:15,970 --> 00:03:16,770
Mum!

68
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:18,370
- Bua!
- Mum!

69
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,600
Mum!

70
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:22,770
- What brings you all here?
- Miss you!

71
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,980
- Miss you too.
- Mummy…

72
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,920
Aw, sweetie.

73
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:28,970
Hello, Aunt Phaka.

74
00:03:29,130 --> 00:03:29,870
Hello.

75
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,020
Hello.

76
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:36,270
So, has this brat caused the Master any trouble, Young Master?

77
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,320
Not at all. She’s been a great help.

78
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,120
Told you, Mum.

79
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,300
How are you doing, Aunt Phaka?

80
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:47,950
I’m good, thank you. Oh, who’s this pretty lady here?

81
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,579
Is she your guest, Young Master?

82
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:55,070
This is Kaphrao. My dad has sent her here to help with work.

83
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:57,380
I see.

84
00:03:58,130 --> 00:04:00,820
Mum, she’s the girl I told you about–my roommate.

85
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,180
- Oh, the one you said she’s very pretty in person?
- Yes!

86
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,250
- That’s her?
- Yes!

87
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,320
Really pretty indeed.

88
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:09,080
I’m Phaka, Bua’s mother.

89
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,100
Hello.

90
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:10,930
Hello.

91
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:16,250
Since you’re already here, come and help me in the kitchen.

92
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:18,579
I’ll prepare something for Young Master.

93
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,399
Geez, Mum.

94
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,329
Stop whining.

95
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:22,470
I’ve just arrived here!

96
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,800
Good luck, girl.

97
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:29,320
Are you going to stay over here tonight? I’ll tell Phaka to prepare the cabin for you.

98
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:32,900
I don’t think so. I’ll just show her around and then we’ll go back.

99
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:34,080
I see.

100
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:39,380
Then, please come eat with us before you leave, okay?

101
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,500
Of course, thank you for inviting us.

102
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,080
Oh, it’s a pleasure.

103
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,750
Enjoy your day then.

104
00:04:49,730 --> 00:04:50,720
Follow me.

105
00:04:57,530 --> 00:04:59,480
How’s it? Got a lot there?

106
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,480
Wow!

107
00:05:10,670 --> 00:05:13,330
Still loves to poke around like when she was seven.

108
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,720
Did you say something?

109
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:17,870
Nothing.

110
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,130
This is my family’s private island.

111
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:27,470
Dad lets the villagers live here for free.

112
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,980
But in return, they must look after the island for us.

113
00:05:31,150 --> 00:05:34,520
It’s so beautiful–so natural.

114
00:05:44,670 --> 00:05:47,570
Be careful, you might get cut. The shells are quite sharp.

115
00:05:48,530 --> 00:05:50,450
Do you think I’m a kid or what?

116
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:55,680
Oh, right! I totally forgot you’re an expert sent by my dad.

117
00:05:56,330 --> 00:06:01,570
Of course, I’m here to work not to pick a fight like someone around here.

118
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:04,900
Anyway, is the princess’s cabin far?

119
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,200
Wanna go back?

120
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:07,750
I was just asking.

121
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:15,150
Hey, what did you do? I saw that.

122
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,720
Are we there yet?

123
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,700
Stop whining or just go back.

124
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,720
We’re here.

125
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:33,650
Wow!

126
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,280
This is Lom and Miss Blew’s cabin.

127
00:06:39,570 --> 00:06:42,520
It holds a lot of their memories.

128
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:44,130
So cute!

129
00:06:49,330 --> 00:06:55,180
That time when the traitors were after Miss Blew, Lom as her bodyguard brought her to hide here.

130
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,750
Wow, that was quite far away.

131
00:06:59,170 --> 00:07:02,750
But those thugs still found out and came after them.

132
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:06,450
Bullets were flying everywhere. They could barely escape just like a scene in an action movie.

133
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:10,480
Lom even got shot and fell into the sea. Fortunately, Miss Blew jumped off the boat to save her.

134
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,950
Otherwise, my sister would’ve turned into a sea ghost.

135
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:16,520
Awesome! You sure know a lot about it.

136
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,280
Because I was there too.

137
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:23,070
Don’t lie.

138
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,500
I’m serious. Why would I lie?

139
00:07:28,670 --> 00:07:31,150
Hey, can I go up and have a look around?

140
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:34,750
Sure, go ahead.

141
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:51,620
Wow, so pretty.

142
00:07:55,530 --> 00:07:56,730
There’s a bed too?

143
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:05,620
And clothes. Does that mean someone lives here?

144
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:07,780
They’re Lom and Miss Blew’s.

145
00:08:08,470 --> 00:08:11,920
They often come here when they have free time. That’s why they’re quite close to the villagers here.

146
00:08:12,470 --> 00:08:13,720
Wow, it’s wonderful.

147
00:08:14,050 --> 00:08:18,880
Look, why don’t we build more cabins like this one?

148
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:22,720
And use the Princess of Madelin’s story as a selling point.

149
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,050
So that visitors who come to stay here would have a similar experience.

150
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:29,850
I’m sure the newly built cabin would look even more amazing.

151
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:33,799
But…

152
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:35,799
But what?

153
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:43,280
If we turn this island into a tourist attraction, I’m afraid it might affect the villagers’ way of living.

154
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:46,680
More visitors means this place will become less peaceful.

155
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,850
I’m surprised you care about other people too.

156
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,950
What? Didn’t you say this island is yours?

157
00:08:56,950 --> 00:08:59,750
I’m afraid you’d just do anything as you please.

158
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:04,320
It’s true that I own this island, but I’m not a selfish person.

159
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:10,020
Unlike someone who only believes that the owner is nothing but a crook.

160
00:09:16,170 --> 00:09:18,950
What else do you think we can use as a selling point?

161
00:09:25,730 --> 00:09:27,420
We have pink seashells here.

162
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,320
Wanna see it?

163
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:53,820
This beach is special. If you find a pink seashell, you’re allowed to make one wish.

164
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:54,770
Really?

165
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:57,620
Yeah, why don’t you try to find one?

166
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:05,280
So silly.

167
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,020
What did you just say?

168
00:10:08,770 --> 00:10:11,350
Look, so many seashells here!

169
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:26,550
Are you sure there’s one? I only see white or cream shells.

170
00:10:29,370 --> 00:10:30,170
Oh!

171
00:10:32,730 --> 00:10:33,850
What colour is it?

172
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:36,750
Are you colour blind? It’s brown!

173
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:48,750
Hey, look! I found it!

174
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:58,680
How’s that possible?

175
00:10:59,020 --> 00:10:59,970
What?

176
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,770
I mean, I didn’t expect you’d find it.

177
00:11:04,530 --> 00:11:06,470
Can I make a wish now?

178
00:11:08,170 --> 00:11:10,720
Yeah, go on.

179
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:17,520
May the project we’re about to do here become successful.

180
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:20,420
And may everyone be happy.

181
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,080
What the hell did you wish for? Look what happens!

182
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,200
I…

183
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,450
What the…?

184
00:11:29,470 --> 00:11:31,120
There’s a cave over there! Let’s go!

185
00:11:41,730 --> 00:11:44,420
Geez! Suddenly pouring down like that?

186
00:11:45,930 --> 00:11:49,020
It’s during the monsoon season. We get more rainy days than sunny ones.

187
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,150
But it’s quick to pass by.

188
00:11:51,770 --> 00:11:55,680
But it’s still pouring buckets. How are we gonna go home then?

189
00:11:57,670 --> 00:12:00,520
We have to wait until it stops, obviously–you nitwit.

190
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,720
Hey, I asked you nicely.

191
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,330
And I answered you nicely too.

192
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,980
But you just called me nitwit–I don’t like it!

193
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,050
You nitwit.

194
00:12:10,050 --> 00:12:11,220
Buffalo Fai!

195
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:22,050
Wait, whose is this?

196
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:33,380
When I want some alone time on the island, I’ll either set up a tent outside or sleep in this cave.

197
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,450
Do you think you’re a hermit or what?

198
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,150
It’s called being indie!

199
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:46,420
Hello?

200
00:12:46,530 --> 00:12:50,480
Hello, Young Master. Where are you right now?

201
00:12:50,730 --> 00:12:53,080
In the cave around the back of an island.

202
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:58,880
The storm just hit and it’s raining so heavily. I’ll go get you there.

203
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:07,580
No need. It’s too dangerous if you come out now. I’ll go back once the rain lets up.

204
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:12,920
Okay then. But if there’s anything unusual, please call me right away, Young Master.

205
00:13:13,530 --> 00:13:15,000
Yes, please don’t worry.

206
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,130
Yes, Young Master.

207
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:27,400
So, when will the rain stop?

208
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:33,680
If it keeps raining, we might have to sleep here.

209
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:36,550
What? Here?

210
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,950
I’m not a hermit like you.

211
00:13:42,970 --> 00:13:45,780
You’re the one who wants to come here in the first place.

212
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:07,950
Hey.

213
00:14:09,170 --> 00:14:10,650
Get changed or you might catch a cold.

214
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:12,680
Into this cave-rotten shirt?

215
00:14:13,730 --> 00:14:15,780
Then go ahead and let yourself freeze to death.

216
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:25,020
Hey! What are you doing?

217
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:26,180
Changing, obviously.

218
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,820
Do it somewhere else then!

219
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:31,880
Look around, where else can I do it? In the middle of the rain?

220
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,080
Geez!

221
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,150
What have I done to get this karma?

222
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,200
Hey.

223
00:14:47,130 --> 00:14:50,020
What? Are you shy?

224
00:14:52,470 --> 00:14:53,580
What? No.

225
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:56,180
But you’re blushing.

226
00:14:57,270 --> 00:14:58,880
We ran a long way from there.

227
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,580
Fine, change into this then.

228
00:15:05,370 --> 00:15:07,950
But if you’re shy, just do it behind that rock.

229
00:15:21,070 --> 00:15:22,150
Are you done?

230
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:24,350
Shut up.

231
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:41,850
You’ll get to sleep in a tent for sure.

232
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:44,180
Go away.

233
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:48,880
Sitting there alone, you might get spooked.

234
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,150
So? I’ll knock its teeth out!

235
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:56,250
Young Master!

236
00:15:56,250 --> 00:15:56,920
Bua!

237
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,250
I’m here!

238
00:16:00,570 --> 00:16:02,850
The rain has let up so Dad told me to come and get you.

239
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:03,800
Here, take it.

240
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:05,270
You too.

241
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:08,300
Let’s go then.

242
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,880
So, it stopped raining just like that? Unbelievable.

243
00:16:24,370 --> 00:16:26,250
The sea in the south is always like that.

244
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:31,080
The storm is pretty bad today. The waves are probably too strong to go offshore.

245
00:16:31,170 --> 00:16:33,720
You’d better stay here tonight, Young Master.

246
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:37,250
What? Does that mean we won’t be able to go back until tomorrow, Bua?

247
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:40,950
I’m not sure either. Sometimes, the storm lasts for days.

248
00:16:42,170 --> 00:16:47,180
Or even three to four days. The worst case I’ve experienced was a week.

249
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,320
Damn it.

250
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:55,950
Please make yourself comfortable then. I’ll go get dinner ready.

251
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:03,480
Don’t you dare make that face, you silly Gremlin.

252
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:07,319
We’re stuck here all because you were being stubborn.

253
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:28,820
Let’s see if Lom has left any clothes here.

254
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,650
Here, change into this.

255
00:17:54,570 --> 00:17:57,620
I’m not using someone else’s belongings without their permission.

256
00:17:57,930 --> 00:18:01,250
If you’re so puffed up with your pride, then just stay rotten in that outfit.

257
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:04,720
I’m going to shower and get changed. We’re stinking like a walking dustbin.

258
00:18:05,650 --> 00:18:07,150
Your face also stinks!

259
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:14,380
If you change your mind, just follow me.

260
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:45,650
Just make it quick, I don’t like to wait. And don’t forget to wash your hair–it got wet from the rain.

261
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,580
You hardly have anything to protect your brain.

262
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:50,520
Then, go shower first so that you won’t keep rushing me.

263
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:53,080
I’ll wait here. Be quick.

264
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,720
You also know how to be nice, huh?

265
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:25,130
Don’t you have anywhere else to stay?

266
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,420
Stop being so fussy, silly Gremlin.

267
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:34,380
Or do you want to go sleep in the cave? Go on then.

268
00:19:35,570 --> 00:19:37,250
I just don’t want to sleep here with you!

269
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,280
As if you’ve never done it before.

270
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:43,950
Back then, I had to throw you out of my room almost every day.

271
00:19:50,670 --> 00:19:51,750
I’m going to sleep.

272
00:19:51,870 --> 00:19:56,080
If you’re going to stay there, just be a guard dog all night.

273
00:20:14,330 --> 00:20:15,580
Is she already asleep?

274
00:20:28,050 --> 00:20:30,570
Damn you! Hogging it all to yourself.

275
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:12,470
Fai and Kaphrao went to the island?

276
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:18,320
Yes. Uncle Boonsong just sent word that Miss Kaphrao wanted to take a look around the island.

277
00:21:18,550 --> 00:21:23,780
But the storm suddenly hit, so both of them have to stay over on the island tonight.

278
00:21:24,870 --> 00:21:26,450
Has anyone told Panee about this?

279
00:21:26,570 --> 00:21:28,420
- She should know it by now.
- Ak!

280
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:31,150
Why did you leave my niece with that girl again?

281
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:36,620
Just you wait. If my niece’s got even a tiny scratch on her, that Athittaya girl must be responsible for it!

282
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,300
Calm down, Panee.

283
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:42,320
Your niece is my daughter too. I’m also worried about her.

284
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:46,720
You’re always taking that girl’s side. You love her more than your own child.

285
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:49,780
It’s because you’re like this, that’s why Fai always gets me wrong!

286
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:51,950
That girl keeps bringing Fai troubles.

287
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:54,180
That’s why I want Fai to stay away from her.

288
00:21:54,370 --> 00:21:58,420
Have you ever asked her if that’s what she wants?

289
00:22:00,730 --> 00:22:06,520
I’ve always chosen the best for her–because I love her the most!

290
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:05,320
Go talk downstairs.

291
00:24:45,270 --> 00:24:46,600
We can go on land today?

292
00:24:47,270 --> 00:24:52,920
Yes, Dad told me to let you know that he’ll leave here before noon to take you and Miss Phrao home.

293
00:24:56,700 --> 00:24:58,680
There isn’t any storm coming today, right?

294
00:24:59,100 --> 00:24:59,900
That’s right.

295
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,770
Then, please go tell Uncle Boonsong this–

296
00:25:10,130 --> 00:25:12,450
Or would you rather leave right now, Young Master?

297
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:14,500
Nope.

298
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:17,800
Okay.

299
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,350
Having a good time?

300
00:25:35,530 --> 00:25:37,450
I thought you’d wake up tomorrow morning.

301
00:25:39,130 --> 00:25:40,530
Get up then.

302
00:25:41,100 --> 00:25:45,250
Stop dawdling and go shower so we can have breakfast.

303
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:50,130
The sky is so bright.

304
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,350
That means we can go back today, right?

305
00:25:54,130 --> 00:25:54,930
Not yet.

306
00:25:55,700 --> 00:25:58,720
Why? The sky is looking so bright today.

307
00:26:00,780 --> 00:26:03,750
No idea. Go ask Uncle Boonsong if you want to know.

308
00:26:04,130 --> 00:26:07,420
But I don’t want to get stuck here anymore. Just one day is more than enough.

309
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,780
So? But you have to stay anyway.

310
00:26:10,070 --> 00:26:12,320
Just blame it on yourself because you didn’t heed my advice.

311
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:16,980
Oh! But if you’re dying to leave here, you can try swimming to shore instead.

312
00:26:16,980 --> 00:26:18,720
If I could, I would’ve done it since yesterday.

313
00:26:18,730 --> 00:26:20,370
Blah, blah, blah!

314
00:26:24,070 --> 00:26:25,320
What a jerk!

315
00:26:33,270 --> 00:26:34,700
[Bua]: Want some crab?

316
00:26:34,700 --> 00:26:35,730
[Boongsong]: Eat all you like.

317
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:38,850
[Phaka]: Go on, dear. I made them especially for you.

318
00:26:38,850 --> 00:26:39,780
[Boonsong]: This is good.

319
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:40,920
[Bua]: Mum’s cooking is the best.

320
00:26:42,770 --> 00:26:44,580
Can’t we go back today?

321
00:26:45,820 --> 00:26:46,870
Sure, you can.

322
00:26:47,570 --> 00:26:48,920
[Bua and Boonsong]: NO!

323
00:26:51,780 --> 00:26:57,420
We can’t do that. We can’t go offshore today. The storm is hitting pretty hard.

324
00:26:57,500 --> 00:26:59,670
But the sky looks so bright to me though.

325
00:27:02,870 --> 00:27:04,320
- Yeah.
- Well,

326
00:27:07,130 --> 00:27:13,320
D…Don’t let the sky fool you. Trust me, the storm is now forming right in the middle of the sea.

327
00:27:13,330 --> 00:27:14,130
Yeah.

328
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,000
Yeah, that’s right.

329
00:27:15,020 --> 00:27:17,170
Look there. It’s so windy, isn’t it?

330
00:27:17,330 --> 00:27:22,180
The wind is so strong even a crab gets blown off the rock.

331
00:27:22,180 --> 00:27:25,520
The crab was so shocked. I saw it with my own eyes, Dad.

332
00:27:27,420 --> 00:27:28,580
- Really?
- Really, Mum.

333
00:27:28,580 --> 00:27:29,950
The crab was shocked?

334
00:27:30,330 --> 00:27:32,420
Yes! You can literally see its eyes wide open.

335
00:27:32,420 --> 00:27:37,450
It was holding on to the rock for life, fighting the strong wind all night long. That’s why.

336
00:27:37,470 --> 00:27:43,480
That’s right. If we leave right now, we might get blown off course and go all the way to Malaysia.

337
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:44,500
We can’t risk it.

338
00:27:44,730 --> 00:27:46,300
Yeah, we’ll get blown away for sure. Can’t risk it.

339
00:27:47,130 --> 00:27:50,600
Once the storm has passed, we’ll be able to leave.

340
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:53,670
That’s right.

341
00:27:55,380 --> 00:27:56,730
Let’s eat.

342
00:27:56,900 --> 00:27:58,480
- Eat all you like, Miss.
- Yeah.

343
00:27:58,500 --> 00:28:04,920
Actually, it’s quite nice being stuck here on the island. It’s giving off such a romantic vibe.

344
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,650
Don’t you think so, Young Master?

345
00:28:10,170 --> 00:28:10,750
Let’s eat.

346
00:28:10,750 --> 00:28:12,620
- Yeah, let’s eat.
- Go on.

347
00:28:13,180 --> 00:28:15,850
[Bua]: Nothing, Mum. Let me get this for you. There.

348
00:28:16,680 --> 00:28:18,050
[Bua]: Here you go.

349
00:28:18,050 --> 00:28:19,020
[Bua]: Dad, what do you want?

350
00:28:19,020 --> 00:28:21,050
[Boonsong]: Kaeng Som*. (*Sour and Spicy Curry)
[Fai miming]: Eat!

351
00:28:21,050 --> 00:28:22,320
[Boonsong]: Thanks.

352
00:28:48,930 --> 00:28:50,780
Quit making a long face.

353
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:53,200
People here might think I’m not treating you well.

354
00:28:53,870 --> 00:28:55,620
But I want to go home.

355
00:28:59,170 --> 00:29:01,580
Tomorrow morning, Uncle Boonsong will take us home.

356
00:29:01,930 --> 00:29:02,880
Really?

357
00:29:04,900 --> 00:29:06,350
Why would I lie?

358
00:29:06,700 --> 00:29:09,080
Finally, I’m going home!

359
00:29:20,130 --> 00:29:25,250
Tell me honestly, do you really hate being stuck here with me that much?

360
00:29:41,420 --> 00:29:45,350
Yes, you also feel the same, don’t you?

361
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:50,800
Of course!

362
00:29:52,070 --> 00:29:55,480
It’s been over 24 hours. I can’t wait to get you out of my face!

363
00:29:55,820 --> 00:29:57,050
So annoying!

364
00:29:57,770 --> 00:30:00,180
Hurry up! Don’t you know it’s rude to keep the older ones waiting?

365
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:01,300
Get up!

366
00:30:09,270 --> 00:30:10,950
What the hell is wrong with her?

367
00:30:27,970 --> 00:30:31,750
Guys, here comes the squid!

368
00:30:31,970 --> 00:30:34,080
- Squid?
- Here you go.

369
00:30:34,080 --> 00:30:37,480
Yes, go ahead and dig in.

370
00:30:37,480 --> 00:30:38,700
Wow, looks yummy.

371
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:42,650
My throat is burning already.

372
00:30:43,130 --> 00:30:45,400
- Easy there.
- It’s burning.

373
00:30:45,770 --> 00:30:49,580
I’m stuck here on this island because of you.

374
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:50,980
It’s all your fault!

375
00:30:51,330 --> 00:30:54,780
Stop saying the same thing over and over again–it’s so annoying!

376
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:58,780
Because you’re stubborn and never listen to a damn thing I say.

377
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:00,070
Say it to yourself first.

378
00:31:00,470 --> 00:31:03,080
You’re getting so wasted you might drown in your own puke.

379
00:31:04,870 --> 00:31:06,250
Drown in my own puke?

380
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:08,750
You really don’t know me, huh?

381
00:31:09,170 --> 00:31:11,750
What a smart mouth. Wanna try it?

382
00:31:11,750 --> 00:31:12,950
Go away. You reek of alcohol!

383
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:15,820
Come on, don’t play innocent.

384
00:31:15,820 --> 00:31:17,650
No! Go away!

385
00:31:17,650 --> 00:31:19,450
There she goes!

386
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:25,080
Here, Young Master. One more.

387
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:26,080
Want some more, babe?

388
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:26,850
No!

389
00:31:27,380 --> 00:31:30,650
What? Chicken out, huh? Does that mean you’re a wimp?

390
00:31:30,650 --> 00:31:31,820
Give it here!

391
00:31:33,050 --> 00:31:34,180
Oh, she’s up for it now.

392
00:31:35,420 --> 00:31:37,250
She’s not a wimp, guys!

393
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:40,320
Here, Young Master. I’ll top it off for you.

394
00:31:40,320 --> 00:31:43,280
Come on, let’s do a round, guys!

395
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:45,150
Just half a glass for you, Mum.

396
00:31:45,150 --> 00:31:47,450
Cheers!

397
00:31:48,450 --> 00:31:49,850
Down it!

398
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:54,480
Loser!

399
00:31:55,220 --> 00:31:57,480
Ha! We’ve just started, babe.

400
00:31:57,480 --> 00:31:58,720
- Bring it on!
- Cheers!

401
00:32:05,250 --> 00:32:07,950
Come then.

402
00:32:08,880 --> 00:32:10,050
Do you dare?

403
00:32:10,050 --> 00:32:10,850
Bring it on.

404
00:32:17,720 --> 00:32:19,750
- Dad and Mum, you do it too.
- Look!

405
00:32:19,750 --> 00:32:20,650
Mine is empty too!

406
00:32:44,220 --> 00:32:46,780
[Kaphrao]: Can you do it?

407
00:32:47,920 --> 00:32:48,750
Watch me!

408
00:32:48,750 --> 00:32:49,880
Come on!

409
00:32:59,300 --> 00:33:00,880
One!

410
00:33:01,120 --> 00:33:02,750
Two!

411
00:33:02,980 --> 00:33:04,950
Three!

412
00:33:04,950 --> 00:33:06,850
Four!

413
00:33:06,850 --> 00:33:08,850
Five!

414
00:33:08,850 --> 00:33:09,780
Ten!

415
00:33:10,650 --> 00:33:14,050
We already count to ten. You lose!

416
00:33:22,970 --> 00:33:27,280
What kind of bar was that? Stop talking nonsense.

417
00:33:27,500 --> 00:33:29,050
It’s you who should stop talking nonsense.

418
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:31,320
Can’t you just walk properly?

419
00:33:31,320 --> 00:33:32,880
I am…

420
00:33:33,270 --> 00:33:34,270
walking so straight.

421
00:33:36,700 --> 00:33:38,280
You’re just all talk.

422
00:33:39,870 --> 00:33:41,580
I’m the best in the world.

423
00:33:42,280 --> 00:33:44,920
Can you please walk properly?

424
00:33:45,500 --> 00:33:47,380
I’m doing it.

425
00:33:47,600 --> 00:33:49,680
Geez, try to be more helpful, will you?

426
00:34:51,730 --> 00:34:54,780
[Young Kaphrao]: Please let me sleep in your room.

427
00:34:54,929 --> 00:34:55,980
Go away!

428
00:34:56,330 --> 00:34:57,870
Please let me sleep in your room, Fai!

429
00:34:57,970 --> 00:34:59,650
But I don’t want to!

430
00:34:59,730 --> 00:35:02,320
But I’ve never slept alone. I’m scared!

431
00:35:04,700 --> 00:35:06,920
Fai, please open the door!

432
00:35:06,920 --> 00:35:08,380
Fai!

433
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:10,220
Fai!

434
00:35:11,100 --> 00:35:13,520
Please open the door!

435
00:35:13,530 --> 00:35:16,220
I’ve never slept alone. I’m scared!

436
00:35:16,600 --> 00:35:18,780
Fai, I’m scared!

437
00:35:18,930 --> 00:35:22,170
Fai, please open the door! I’m scared!

438
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:24,770
Fai, I’m scared!

439
00:35:26,170 --> 00:35:30,280
Fai! I’m scared, Fai!

440
00:35:30,530 --> 00:35:32,480
I’ve never slept alone!

441
00:35:32,770 --> 00:35:35,480
You nitwit! Are you going to stand here and cry all night?

442
00:35:35,500 --> 00:35:37,980
If you don’t stop crying, I will not let you in.

443
00:36:02,330 --> 00:36:07,420
Go sleep over there. If you touch me, I’ll throw you out of here.

444
00:36:07,780 --> 00:36:09,050
Got it?

445
00:36:10,270 --> 00:36:11,070
Yes.

446
00:37:21,500 --> 00:37:23,550
Do you hate me that much?

447
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:37,220
I'm sorry.

448
00:39:25,700 --> 00:39:26,880
What the heck? What did you do?

449
00:39:27,100 --> 00:39:28,180
What? I didn’t do anything!

450
00:39:28,300 --> 00:39:30,250
You were so drunk last night.

451
00:39:32,930 --> 00:39:35,220
So what? Did we sleep together?

452
00:39:35,300 --> 00:39:37,370
Are you nuts? How could you say something like that?

453
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:39,150
That hurts!

454
00:39:39,700 --> 00:39:42,420
You’re hurting me, Gremlin!

455
00:39:42,420 --> 00:39:44,050
It hurts! Stop!

456
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:47,020
That’s because you said something disgusting! Gross!

457
00:39:47,130 --> 00:39:48,370
Look who’s talking.

458
00:39:48,570 --> 00:39:50,870
I know you tried to take advantage of me last night, didn’t you?

459
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:51,900
I didn’t do it!

460
00:39:52,020 --> 00:39:56,120
Are you sure? I woke up and your arm was wrapping around me.

461
00:39:57,950 --> 00:40:00,450
It was you who got drunk and tried to molest me last night.

462
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:02,420
Don’t be ridiculous. Do you have proof?

463
00:40:02,620 --> 00:40:04,580
I do though–with my own eyes.

464
00:40:04,580 --> 00:40:06,480
I don’t fancy you for even one bit!

465
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:08,850
Ha! As if I were too!

466
00:40:08,870 --> 00:40:10,020
Fine! Whatever!

467
00:40:10,130 --> 00:40:12,580
Go then! What are you waiting for?

468
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:23,650
[Hold On Together Shop]

469
00:40:37,320 --> 00:40:39,650
Oh, you’re here? How are you feeling, Young Master?

470
00:40:39,950 --> 00:40:41,180
Have you sobered up now?

471
00:40:41,620 --> 00:40:42,620
Yes, much better.

472
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:45,250
Young Master! Young Master!

473
00:40:45,250 --> 00:40:46,720
Wait for me too.

474
00:40:49,020 --> 00:40:50,980
I thought you wouldn’t go back with us this time.

475
00:40:51,530 --> 00:40:52,470
I wouldn’t miss it.

476
00:40:55,070 --> 00:40:57,080
- Dad, Mum…
- What now?

477
00:40:57,200 --> 00:40:58,480
I’m leaving.

478
00:40:58,480 --> 00:41:00,280
- Look at her.
- Aren’t you staying?

479
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:02,720
Stop complaining. Give me a hug!

480
00:41:03,470 --> 00:41:05,480
Love you, Dad!

481
00:41:05,600 --> 00:41:07,820
- You too, Mum.
- Come, dear.

482
00:41:09,170 --> 00:41:10,750
I wonder who she’s taking after.

483
00:41:10,750 --> 00:41:12,180
Her mother, of course.

484
00:41:13,450 --> 00:41:19,820
I promise that next time when I come back, I’ll bring you sons-in-law–how about ten of them?

485
00:41:19,820 --> 00:41:21,980
- Whoa!
- As you wish!

486
00:41:21,980 --> 00:41:23,320
Hey, don’t encourage her!

487
00:41:23,730 --> 00:41:26,670
Who cares? If she wants to, just let her be.

488
00:41:26,970 --> 00:41:32,250
But make sure you do your work for Young Master too. Don’t just go flirting around and cause her trouble.

489
00:41:32,250 --> 00:41:32,780
I know, Mum.

490
00:41:32,780 --> 00:41:34,420
Bring me three or four, maybe.

491
00:41:34,420 --> 00:41:35,250
You got it.

492
00:41:35,250 --> 00:41:36,620
Bring one for me too.

493
00:41:37,250 --> 00:41:39,080
Don’t even think about it.

494
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,480
Geez, I was just kidding.

495
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:45,180
Miss Kaphrao, please come visit us again.

496
00:41:45,270 --> 00:41:48,020
Of course. If I have a chance, I’ll definitely drop by.

497
00:41:48,020 --> 00:41:50,350
This place is really nice and so beautiful.

498
00:41:51,500 --> 00:41:54,720
Don’t worry, you’ll get to come here again for sure.

499
00:41:56,280 --> 00:42:00,520
Dad wants you to help me with this project, you’ll get to come here until you’re sick of it.

500
00:42:01,500 --> 00:42:04,320
If it’s about work, I’ll never back down.

501
00:42:04,930 --> 00:42:05,820
Good!

502
00:42:10,700 --> 00:42:12,450
Let’s go then. The sun is getting stronger.

503
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:15,650
Hey, not so fast!

504
00:42:15,650 --> 00:42:18,950
- Don’t run, dear. You might trip over.
- Silly girl.

505
00:42:19,250 --> 00:42:20,880
Exactly like her mother.

506
00:42:21,150 --> 00:42:22,620
Stop talking nonsense!

507
00:42:22,620 --> 00:42:23,480
Be careful!

508
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:25,120
Don’t worry, Dad! This is nothing.

509
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:43,800
That’s all right. I can manage.

510
00:42:44,570 --> 00:42:48,200
Come on. I don’t want you to have an excuse to complain to my dad if you fall off the boat.

511
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:50,100
Hurry up.

512
00:43:04,450 --> 00:43:11,720
♫I could never forget those eyes of yours♫

513
00:43:11,720 --> 00:43:18,050
♫The warmth you used to give me, I still remember it vividly♫

514
00:43:18,550 --> 00:43:25,480
♫No matter for how long, you’ll always remain in my heart♫

515
00:43:25,480 --> 00:43:34,920
♫All those years I’ve been waiting, for us to finally be together again♫

516
00:43:36,730 --> 00:43:38,880
Good luck!

517
00:43:38,970 --> 00:43:40,920
- Bye Bye!
- Have a safe trip.

518
00:43:40,930 --> 00:43:42,370
Please take care of yourself!

519
00:43:42,570 --> 00:43:43,370
Okay.

520
00:43:43,700 --> 00:43:45,850
I’ll bring you a son-in-law next time!

521
00:43:48,170 --> 00:43:49,580
Good luck, dear.

522
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:52,980
They’re gone.

523
00:43:56,550 --> 00:43:57,600
Our rascal Bua.

524
00:44:01,300 --> 00:44:05,550
Bye, dear! Good luck!

525
00:44:12,470 --> 00:44:13,880
Fai is back?

526
00:44:14,100 --> 00:44:18,670
Yes. But right now, she’s discussing work with the Master and Miss Kaphrao.

527
00:44:20,070 --> 00:44:22,770
My niece has just got back from a long trip, what’s there to talk about?

528
00:44:23,600 --> 00:44:27,350
No idea too. But it probably won’t take long. She’ll be home soon.

529
00:44:36,670 --> 00:44:38,620
What should we have for dinner, Miss Phrao?

530
00:44:38,730 --> 00:44:40,270
I’ll let you choose today.

531
00:44:40,400 --> 00:44:41,020
Sure.

532
00:44:41,020 --> 00:44:42,420
Athittaya.

533
00:44:46,900 --> 00:44:51,020
Haven’t I warned you not to cause Fai any trouble?

534
00:44:51,600 --> 00:44:54,520
If it’s about getting stuck on the island, I can explain.

535
00:44:54,520 --> 00:44:59,450
Don’t talk back to me! You’re as rude as ever.

536
00:45:01,200 --> 00:45:04,220
Miss Panee, the storm was terrible indeed.

537
00:45:04,220 --> 00:45:05,820
We couldn’t leave the island–as if the sky were tumbling–

538
00:45:05,820 --> 00:45:11,720
Who asked you? Don’t butt in. Just get lost.

539
00:45:12,730 --> 00:45:13,530
Yes, Miss.

540
00:45:16,700 --> 00:45:21,320
You put my niece in trouble and also in danger.

541
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:25,670
I’m sorry.

542
00:45:25,870 --> 00:45:26,770
Sorry again?

543
00:45:27,770 --> 00:45:29,880
I’m sick of hearing this word from you.

544
00:45:32,800 --> 00:45:35,250
Then, what do you want me to do?

545
00:45:43,870 --> 00:45:45,330
You ask for it yourself.

546
00:46:12,570 --> 00:46:14,150
Young Master, please stop!

547
00:46:14,150 --> 00:46:15,220
Please stop!

548
00:46:17,470 --> 00:46:18,450
What is it, Bua?

549
00:46:18,470 --> 00:46:21,520
Young Master, you…

550
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:23,070
you need to help Miss Phrao.

551
00:46:23,200 --> 00:46:26,280
Miss Panee is so mad at Miss Phrao for taking you away from her for many days.

552
00:46:26,400 --> 00:46:28,020
So, she punishes her.

553
00:46:28,530 --> 00:46:29,480
Is it that bad?

554
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:33,250
Yes, you need to go talk to Miss Panee and help Miss Phrao.

555
00:46:33,400 --> 00:46:35,080
I feel bad for her.

556
00:46:36,470 --> 00:46:38,380
I don’t think she’d listen to me.

557
00:46:38,730 --> 00:46:39,780
Young Master!

558
00:46:41,170 --> 00:46:43,770
But don’t worry. I’ll find a way to help her.

559
00:46:54,700 --> 00:46:56,470
Panee punishes my Little One?

560
00:46:56,730 --> 00:46:58,580
Yes, she’s in the garden right now.

561
00:48:00,100 --> 00:48:02,220
At this rate, you’ll probably finish it next year.

562
00:48:02,270 --> 00:48:03,420
What are you doing?

563
00:48:04,270 --> 00:48:07,050
Cooking, maybe? Wanna eat it?

564
00:48:07,970 --> 00:48:10,450
If Miss Panee sees us together, she’ll be more furious.

565
00:48:10,570 --> 00:48:12,720
I already have a lot on my shoulders.

566
00:48:12,720 --> 00:48:14,950
Please don’t make it worse for me.

567
00:48:16,670 --> 00:48:19,220
It’s also my fault that you got punished.

568
00:48:19,270 --> 00:48:21,150
So, I’ll take half of the punishment too.

569
00:48:34,780 --> 00:48:38,150
What are you looking at? Go scoop up the grass!

570
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,470
Back then, it was you, wasn’t it?

571
00:49:01,700 --> 00:49:07,650
Pluck out all the weeds. Don’t go home if you can’t finish it.

572
00:49:45,130 --> 00:49:51,120
Phrao. It’s lunchtime. Let’s eat, dear.

573
00:49:52,000 --> 00:49:52,870
Are you tired?

574
00:50:23,700 --> 00:50:24,800
How is this possible?

575
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:38,080
Back then when I got punished, you were the one who helped me, weren’t you?

576
00:50:42,330 --> 00:50:45,850
I didn’t do anything wrong back then. Why would I help you?

577
00:50:47,400 --> 00:50:52,980
Then, if you know that person who used to help me, can you please say ‘thank you’ to her for me?

578
00:50:57,600 --> 00:50:58,780
Can’t do that.

579
00:51:00,130 --> 00:51:01,250
Thank you.

580
00:51:01,770 --> 00:51:03,420
I said I can’t do that.

581
00:51:03,600 --> 00:51:05,350
That was for you.

582
00:51:21,120 --> 00:51:23,880
♫But then who are you?♫

583
00:51:23,880 --> 00:51:27,780
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

584
00:51:27,780 --> 00:51:30,350
♫Please tell me♫

585
00:51:30,350 --> 00:51:33,580
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

586
00:51:33,580 --> 00:51:36,850
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

587
00:51:36,850 --> 00:51:39,880
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

588
00:51:39,880 --> 00:51:43,120
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

589
00:51:43,120 --> 00:51:46,350
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

590
00:51:46,350 --> 00:51:49,580
Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

591
00:51:49,580 --> 00:51:52,820
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

592
00:51:52,820 --> 00:51:55,820
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

593
00:51:55,930 --> 00:51:56,770
♫Is it you?♫

594
00:52:03,570 --> 00:52:04,980
Stop, stop.

595
00:52:08,170 --> 00:52:10,900
Go that way! There’re still lots of weeds there.

596
00:52:12,370 --> 00:52:15,650
Fai is here to help my Little One. There’s nothing to worry about now.

597
00:52:16,980 --> 00:52:19,020
It’s a good sign, isn’t it?

598
00:52:20,670 --> 00:52:27,080
I hope things will get even better in the future–as it should’ve been a long time ago.

599
00:52:27,700 --> 00:52:28,500
Let's go.

600
00:52:30,670 --> 00:52:31,620
Fai.

601
00:52:31,620 --> 00:52:35,120
The ground is dirty, don’t just lie down like that? Get up.

602
00:52:35,800 --> 00:52:38,570
I’m totally beat. Let me stay like this for a while.

603
00:52:42,730 --> 00:52:44,170
I did most of the work there.

604
00:52:46,570 --> 00:52:48,670
So? I didn’t ask for your help.

605
00:52:49,470 --> 00:52:53,170
You were so slow. If you’d done it alone, it would’ve taken years to finish it.

606
00:52:54,800 --> 00:52:57,700
Fine, go on and stay like that. I’m leaving.

607
00:52:59,170 --> 00:53:04,220
Hey, are you really going to leave me here? I came to help you.

608
00:53:07,500 --> 00:53:09,720
Then, get up. Get up!

609
00:53:23,280 --> 00:53:26,720
♫Those times we used to be happy together♫

610
00:53:26,720 --> 00:53:30,720
♫I still cherish every minute of them♫

611
00:53:30,720 --> 00:53:35,950
♫But I don't know if you also feel the same♫

612
00:53:36,320 --> 00:53:42,380
♫Those things in the past, I still can’t forget them♫

613
00:53:42,380 --> 00:53:48,750
♫I want to know if you’re like that too–do you also feel the same?♫

614
00:53:49,150 --> 00:53:56,350
♫I could never forget those eyes of yours♫

615
00:53:56,350 --> 00:54:02,780
♫The warmth you used to give me, I still remember it vividly♫

616
00:54:03,380 --> 00:54:04,920
♫No matter for how long…♫

617
00:54:04,930 --> 00:54:07,800
[Next Episode]
I also ordered Nambang chicken for you.

618
00:54:08,370 --> 00:54:10,620
Aunt Panee made me go on a blind date this morning.

619
00:54:10,900 --> 00:54:11,800
How was it?

620
00:54:12,170 --> 00:54:14,970
Don’t you feel anything at all that I went out with someone else?

621
00:54:15,200 --> 00:54:17,720
I was going to give you some advice on how to pursue a girl.

622
00:54:18,380 --> 00:54:20,450
So, what should I do?

623
00:54:20,930 --> 00:54:22,650
Do you want to go to the dam with me?

624
00:54:24,100 --> 00:54:24,900
The dam?

625
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:28,850
You’ve been acting strange lately.

626
00:54:32,130 --> 00:54:36,050
Now that I’ve met Phrao again, I’ll never let her go.

627
00:54:36,550 --> 00:54:38,050
I like you, Kaphrao.

628
00:54:38,320 --> 00:54:39,950
I like her too.

629
00:54:59,550 --> 00:55:06,580
♫I still remember vividly that day when we first met♫

630
00:55:07,150 --> 00:55:12,950
♫Those memories we had together never fade away from my heart♫

631
00:55:13,320 --> 00:55:20,920
♫We might never say it out loud how we feel for each other♫

632
00:55:20,920 --> 00:55:26,650
♫But deep down we both know how we feel♫

633
00:55:26,650 --> 00:55:32,780
♫Those things in the past, I still can’t forget them♫

634
00:55:32,780 --> 00:55:38,920
♫I want to know if you’re like that too–do you also feel the same?♫

635
00:55:39,320 --> 00:55:46,850
♫I could never forget those eyes of yours♫

636
00:55:46,850 --> 00:55:53,320
♫The warmth you used to give me, I still remember it vividly♫

637
00:55:53,580 --> 00:56:00,650
♫No matter for how long, you’ll always remain in my heart♫

638
00:56:00,650 --> 00:56:11,050
♫All those years I’ve been waiting, for us to finally be together again♫

639
00:56:19,120 --> 00:56:22,980
[North Star Entertainment]

640
00:56:22,980 --> 00:56:26,980
[Flaming Chains of Love]
